<title>UK: TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS TEAM EVENT RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS TEAM EVENT RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of team</p>
<p>event matches on the fourth day of the world table tennis</p>
<p>championships on Sunday: </p>
<p>Men's second round (round-robin matches):</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p>Portugal beat Qatar 3-0</p>
<p>Iran beat Ireland 3-2</p>
<p>Switzerland beat Malaysia 3-0</p>
<p>Group H</p>
<p>Scotland beat Togo 3-0</p>
<p>Bosnia beat Pakistan 3-1</p>
<p>Brazil beat Estonia 3-1</p>
<p>Group J</p>
<p>Latvia beat Moldova 3-2</p>
<p>Argentina beat Philippines 3-2</p>
<p>Lithuania beat Cameroon 3-2</p>
<p>Group K</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia beat Aruba 3-0</p>
<p>Chile beat Barbados 3-0</p>
<p>Kazakhstan beat Panama 3-0</p>
<p>Men's second round crossover section 1/2:</p>
<p>Greece beat United States 3-1</p>
<p>Canada beat Wales 3-0</p>
<p>Egypt beat Finland 3-1</p>
<p>Spain beat Ukraine 3-1</p>
<p>Note: Greece play Canada and Egypt play Spain in crossover</p>
<p>section 3/4 with winners to play third and fourth-placed teams</p>
<p>in Group A.</p>
<p>Women's second round crossover section 3/4 (to decide</p>
<p>remaining quarter-finalists):</p>
